    "current_example": {
      "math_academy_id": "e-3243",
      "problem": "Given that $\\tan\\theta = \\dfrac{1}{4},$ find the value of $x.$\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14244094/assets/f8affbac78c75000d7bbbc8c15508252f7bea0270fdf6cc9c5e5244eb89b505d.png)",
      "worked_solution": "The tangent of an angle is equal to the opposite divided by the adjacent (T-O-A).\n\nRelative to the angle $\\theta,$ the length of the opposite side is $x-1,$ and the length of the adjacent side is $2x.$ Therefore, \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{tan}⁡\\theta  & =\\frac{\\text{opposite}}{\\text{adjacent}} \\\\ \\frac{1}{4} & =\\frac{x-1}{2x} \\\\ 2x & =4(x-1) \\\\ 2x & =4x-4 \\\\ 2x & =4 \\\\ x & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "html_path": "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14244094/observations/step-e3243-bd0c94340e8461f1dac3.html",
